.TH LUMOS 1 "2026-11" "lumos 0.2.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
lumos \- terminal mapper for Nmap evidence
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B lumos
[\fIPATH\fR] [\fB\-\-no\-plugins\fR]
.br
.B lumos
\fICOMMAND\fR [\fIOPTIONS\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B lumos
stores Nmap evidence in an SQLite engagement database, draws the topology in a
terminal interface, and distinguishes what was measured from what was inferred.
Running
.B lumos
with no arguments opens the most recent engagement; running it with a path opens
that database. The interface is mouse-first: drag to pan, wheel to zoom, click to
select.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B lumos db init \fIPATH\fR
Create an empty engagement database.
.TP
.B lumos interfaces
Show the scanner interfaces and routes Nmap reports with \fB--iflist\fR.
.TP
.B lumos tui \fIDB\fR
Open the interactive map explicitly (plain text output when redirected).
.TP
.B lumos scope \fIDB\fR
List, add or remove scope rules. Every scan is checked against them.
.TP
.B lumos scan \fIDB\fR \fITARGET\fR...
Run a scope-checked enumerator and store the result.
.TP
.B lumos import \fIDB\fR \fIFILE.xml\fR
Import Nmap XML, which is parsed as hostile input.
.TP
.B lumos report \fIFORMAT\fR \fIDB\fR \fIOUT\fR
Write markdown, svg, json, csv, html, dot, mermaid or stored nmap-xml
(\fB\-\-scan\fR \fIID\fR).
.TP
.B lumos compare \fIDB\fR
Diff two scans by address.
.TP
.B lumos note \fIDB\fR \fB\-\-body\fR \fITEXT\fR
Add an append-only note to the engagement, a node or an edge.
.TP
.B lumos tag \fIDB\fR \fB\-\-name\fR \fINAME\fR
Tag the engagement, a node or an edge.
.TP
.B lumos review \fIDB\fR
Work the review queue; inferred items are never presented as measured.
.TP
.B lumos manual \fIDB\fR \fB\-\-add\fR \fILABEL\fR | \fB\-\-link\fR \fIFROM\fR \fITO\fR
Record nodes and links the scanner cannot see. They survive every rebuild.
.TP
.B lumos duplicates \fIDB\fR [\fB\-\-accept\fR \fIID\fR | \fB\-\-reject\fR \fIID\fR]
Review duplicate-device proposals. Lumos never merges identity on its own.
.TP
.B lumos export \fIDB\fR \fIOUT\fR
Write a pseudonymised copy: documentation-range addresses, \fI.example\fR
hostnames, rewritten evidence. The source is untouched.
.TP
.B lumos demo \fIOUT\fR
Write a generated engagement for documentation and screenshots. No real data.
.TP
.B lumos plugins
List exporter and theme plugins that would load, and every refusal.
.TP
.B lumos queue \fIDB\fR
Queue scans and run them in order.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/lumos/plugins
Plugin directory (exporter and theme modules).
.TP
.I ~/.config/lumos/profiles.json
Additional scan profiles.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B LUMOS_PLUGIN_PATH
Path-separated plugin directories.
.TP
.B LUMOS_NO_PLUGINS
Any truthy value disables plugins.
.TP
.B LUMOS_PROFILES
Alternative scan-profile file.
.TP
.B LUMOS_THEME
Starting theme name.
.TP
.B NO_COLOR
Forces the monochrome theme.
.SH EXIT STATUS
0 success, 2 refused or invalid input, 130 interrupted.
.SH SEE ALSO
Nmap(1), and the documentation in the source tree: README.md, docs/PLUGINS.md,
docs/ZENMAP-PARITY.md, docs/adr/.
